# 05 Match-time options: PCRE2_NOTBOL, NOTEOL, NOTEMPTY,
#    NOTEMPTY_ATSTART, ANCHORED, ENDANCHORED
# https://www.pcre.org/current/doc/html/pcre2api.html
#
# Not exposed by PHP.
#
# What it is: per-call options on pcre2_match() that change how one
# match runs against one subject without touching the compiled pattern.
# NOTBOL says the buffer's start is not the real line start. NOTEOL says
# its end is not the real end. NOTEMPTY and NOTEMPTY_ATSTART refuse empty
# matches. ANCHORED and ENDANCHORED pin the match to the start or the end.
# PHP can bake the A modifier into a pattern but has nothing per call.
#
# What it enables: matching a window of a larger text without lying to
# ^ and $. Also scanners that suppress empty matches instead of
# hand-advancing offsets, and exact-position checks with an unmodified
# pattern.

# Expect: No match
# NOTBOL: the buffer starts mid-line, so ^ must not match at offset 0.
/^a/
    abc\=notbol

# Expect: No match
# NOTEOL: the buffer ends mid-line, so $ must not match at the end.
/c$/
    abc\=noteol

# Expect: 0:
# Baseline for the next block: a* returns an EMPTY match at the start of
# a subject with no 'a' in reach.
/a*/
    bcd

# Expect: No match
# NOTEMPTY: the same call refuses empty matches entirely.
/a*/
    bcd\=notempty

# Expect: 0: aa
# NOTEMPTY_ATSTART refuses only the empty match at the start position.
# The engine moves on and finds the real "aa" instead of returning "" at 0.
/a*/
    xaay\=notempty_atstart

# Expect: No match
# ANCHORED at match time: the match must start exactly at the start
# offset.
/b/
    ab\=anchored

# Expect: 0: b
# The same pattern and subject without the option.
/b/
    ab

# Expect: No match
# ENDANCHORED: the match must END at the end of the subject.
/abc/
    abcdef\=endanchored

# Expect: 0: abc
# Without it, the same match succeeds at the front.
/abc/
    abcdef
